Change to OCCT (V8_0_1) for the Open CAD Viewer. Applied by wasm/scripts/build-occt.sh.

- BRepMesh: the cone seam splitter (BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor) picked the seam edge's pcurve by
  evaluating it at FirstParameter(), which is infinite for a line pcurve. A seam line with a tiny
  tilt (direction X -1.7e-16 in an Autodesk Inventor STEP file) then landed far off, the pcurves were
  swapped, and the seam's inner points were inserted on the opposite seam. The wire crossed
  itself and most of the cone face was left unmeshed. Now evaluated at a parameter of the edge.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx
index 6f637819..6d054665 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx
@@ -223,10 +223,11 @@ private:
       return false;
     }
 
-    // Select the correct pcurve of the seam-edge.
-    const gp_Pnt2d& aFPntOfPC1 = aPC1->Value(aPC1->FirstParameter());
+    // Select the correct pcurve of the seam-edge. Evaluate it at a parameter of the edge:
+    // FirstParameter() of a line pcurve is infinite, and any tilt of the line moves that point.
+    const gp_Pnt2d aFPntOfPC1 = aPC1->Value(aIPC1->GetParameter(0));
 
-    if (std::abs(aLPntOfIPC1.X() - aFPntOfPC1.X()) > Precision::Confusion())
+    if (std::abs(aFPntOfIPC1.X() - aFPntOfPC1.X()) > Precision::Confusion())
     {
       std::swap(aPC1, aPC2);
     }
